# What `dart pub publish` must not put inside the self_test archive.
#
# A `.pubignore` REPLACES `.gitignore` for packaging, it does not add to it, so
# everything git ignores has to be repeated here. Leaving it out is not a
# cosmetic mistake: with only the monorepo rules below, the archive went from
# 2 MB to 36 MB because every build artifact git hides came back.

# --- The reason this file exists -------------------------------------------
# The root pubspec sits at the top of a monorepo, so without this the core
# package ships every sibling package with it: the bridge, the inspector, the
# DevTools extension source and the MCP server's Node tree, none of which is
# any use to someone who installed self_test.
#
# Listed one by one rather than as `packages/`, and that is not tidiness. An
# ignore file applies to every package published from underneath it, so
# `packages/` hid self_test_gen from its OWN `dart pub publish`: the dry run
# came back with an empty archive and "The pubspec is hidden, probably by
# .gitignore or pubignore". self_test_gen is the one sibling that publishes,
# so it is the one that must not be named here. The cost is its 7 KB of source
# riding along inside the core archive, which is the cheaper wart.
packages/self_test_bridge/
packages/self_test_devtools_extension/
packages/self_test_inspector/
packages/self_test_mcp/

# The example is published (pana scores it, and it is the quickstart), but
# only the parts a reader opens. The platform scaffolding is `flutter create`
# output and nobody reads it from pub.dev.
example/android/
example/ios/
example/linux/
example/macos/
example/windows/
example/web/

# Monorepo wiring. It points at ../packages, which this file just removed from
# the archive, so publishing it would hand a reader an example that cannot
# resolve. Its pubspec.yaml already declares the constraints a real consumer
# writes, which is the point of keeping the two files apart.
example/pubspec_overrides.yaml

# --- Repeated from .gitignore ----------------------------------------------
.dart_tool/
**/.dart_tool/
build/
**/doc/api/
**/pubspec.lock
**/.flutter-plugins
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/package-lock.json
.tasks/
.claude/
*.class
*.log
*.pyc
*.swp
.DS_Store
.atom/
.buildlog/
.history
.svn/
migrate_working_dir/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.idea/

# --- Exceptions, same as .gitignore ----------------------------------------
# `extension/devtools/` is how pub.dev and DevTools discover the panel, so the
# built bundle has to travel inside this archive even though `build/` above
# would otherwise drop it. canvaskit stays out: it is 31 MB of the bundle and
# DevTools serves its own copy.
!extension/devtools/build/
!extension/devtools/build/**
extension/devtools/build/canvaskit/
